From: mpv-Yaozhi build adaptation
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/demux: use custom IO close callback on open failure

Backport the functional hunk of FFmpeg dc74fe70b28df8ff69f99b693665163bf9a6a16a
(https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/dc74fe70b28df8ff69f99b693665163bf9a6a16a).
Keep the fork ABI version 62.13.102: do not claim a different upstream minor.
Applied after the existing AV3A/DV patches; no other decoder or demux change.

diff --git a/libavformat/demux.c b/libavformat/demux.c
--- a/libavformat/demux.c
+++ b/libavformat/demux.c
@@ -368,7 +368,7 @@ fail:
     ff_id3v2_free_extra_meta(&id3v2_extra_meta);
     av_dict_free(&tmp);
     if (s->pb && !(s->flags & AVFMT_FLAG_CUSTOM_IO))
-        avio_closep(&s->pb);
+        ff_format_io_close(s, &s->pb);
     avformat_free_context(s);
     *ps = NULL;
     return ret;
